  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Generating the feature plan from a validated specification
    Given the specification describes a feature with several distinct pieces of work
    When the architect_feature_plan session runs to completion
    Then a feature definition, its task documents, and a plan document are returned as one artifact set
    And the feature definition conforms to the pinned feature/task/wave contract
    And the feature definition passes the deterministic validate oracle when written into a repository alongside its task documents

  # Why: Wave detection is the plan's load-bearing structure — dependencies
  # decide sequencing, independence decides parallelism.
  @task:TASK-SPL8-003
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Waves are derived from task dependencies
    Given the plan contains tasks where some depend on the outputs of others
    When the feature definition is generated
    Then every task that depends on another appears in a later wave than that dependency
    And tasks with no dependency relationship may share a wave
    And every task appears in exactly one wave

  # Why: Task frontmatter is the CoachValidator's routing input — a task
  # without a valid type gets the wrong quality gates downstream.
  @task:TASK-SPL8-003
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Every task document carries the required frontmatter
    When the feature definition is generated
    Then every task document declares a task type from the pinned valid set
    And every task document carries the feature identifier that groups it with its siblings
    And every task entry in the feature definition names a task document path under the tasks directory

  # Why: Seam v1.1 — same pinned-data posture as the spec tool; the plan
